[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478525774","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99268#issuecomment-2478525774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99268","id":2478525774,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tu01O","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T10:39:10Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T10:39:10Z","body":"I want to note, `volume_linear` as a concept has been talked about on-and-off, but no one really made a PR about it until now.\r\nOne simple argument in favour of adding this new property is the fact that `rotation_degrees` exists. That's pretty much it, but it's a very strong one because users are expecting this kind of property to exist.\r\nIn fact, back in 4.0's beta, [`rotation_degrees` was removed](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/50009) in favour of `rotation` itself displaying as degrees in the Inspector. [The property was later restored due to backlash](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/70263).\r\nHowever, it's worth keeping in mind that was a whole different case. The code workaround was simple, but script readability and intuitiveness suffered drastically for being such a common operation. A property **that already existed** was removed and re-added for being too useful.\r\n\r\nSo my question is, do users need this commonly enough?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478525774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478793865","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99268#issuecomment-2478793865","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99268","id":2478793865,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tv2SJ","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T13:17:45Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T13:17:45Z","body":"I have a lot of silly code in my commercial game project that wraps `volume_db` so I can control it in linear volume space. So yes, this would be a fantastic addition!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478793865/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2480074771","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99268#issuecomment-2480074771","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99268","id":2480074771,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T0vAT","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T22:47:03Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T23:38:28Z","body":"The two big use cases I see for `volume_linear` personally are fading music in or out with tweens (a pretty standard operation when you have music) and volume sliders (a standard setting in games these days).\r\n\r\nI really love the power of the tweening engine, and I think it could work very well for fading music in and out, but as it is right now with only `volume_db` as a property to access, the code is a mess as described in the original PR post. While it's not as extreme as the tweening case, the user-code overhead for a volume slider feels a bit unnecessary.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I don't think I can recall a single time where I was writing code to control volume, and actually wanted to work in decibels; the tasks I wanted to accomplish always necessitated converting to and/or from a linear scale anyways. My sentiment on this is very close to what [aXu-AP said here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/1884#issuecomment-1765897456) - behavior like setting and adjusting a volume percentage feels like something common enough that we shouldn't have to add in a snippet of code to get it on each individual project.\r\n\r\nI've asked around a little bit for others' experiences on this, and have gotten varied responses: some have said they *always* use a linear scale and don't know why a decibel property would even be exposed, others said that having both would be the best option, and others yet said they hated linear scale. Most of the pushback I saw to the linear scale seemed to be more in the context of sound effects and dialogue, rather than music or overall audio, which is where I think the linear property would shine the most.\r\n\r\nAs for the general sentiment towards a feature like this: the original proposal post has (at the time of writing this) 18 👍 reactions and only one 👎 reaction. Replies to the proposal supporting it have consistently more positive reactions (22ish) than replies that were dismissive of it (3ish). I'd generally point to the proposal thread for peoples' discussions and opinions on adding such a feature.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2480074771/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481775448","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99268#issuecomment-2481775448","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99268","id":2481775448,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T7ONY","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-18T02:03:25Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T02:03:25Z","body":"It did occur to me that `position` and `global_position` are another pair of properties that ultimately modify the same underlying information (where the node is in the world) but within different contexts, so that the appropriate one for a given task can be used.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOops, looks like the `volume_linear` property is being saved to scene files (I opened this project with the feature branch, then again with the master branch, and just noticed it removed this line).\r\n\r\n![CleanShot 2024-11-17 at 18 00 33@2x](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2202397-c5a0-4049-8ae2-7eb4653152d9)\r\n\r\nThat definitely doesn't make sense 😅 Will have to take a look at that and how to fix it in the future before a potential merge.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481775448/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2482940287","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99268#issuecomment-2482940287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99268","id":2482940287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T_ql_","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-18T12:44:17Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T12:44:17Z","body":"It's because of `PROPERTY_USAGE_NO_EDIT`.\r\nIf you want the property to be non-serializable and not editable in the inspector, you should use `PROPERTY_USAGE_NONE`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2482940287/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2486338835","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99268#issuecomment-2486338835","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99268","id":2486338835,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UMoUT","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-19T17:33:16Z","updated_at":"2024-11-19T17:33:16Z","body":"`PROPERTY_USAGE_NO_EDIT` has been changed to `PROPERTY_USAGE_NONE` to avoid the serialization :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2486338835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2556122056","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99268#issuecomment-2556122056","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99268",